    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; the other two files are the base class and an audit-log helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that creating an owner whose lower-cased email already belongs to another owner is rejected with **409 Conflict**, following the repository's established \"duplicate-field\" pattern exactly.\n\nChanges (3 files, each edit small and self-contained):\n\n1. **New `DuplicateEmailException`** (`rest/advice/DuplicateEmailException.java`) \u2014 mirrors `DuplicateTelephoneException`: a static `rejectIfDuplicate(email, existingOwners)` that lower-cases both sides and throws on a match. A blank/absent candidate email is treated as \"not in use\" and never rejected.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added a tiny `handleDuplicateEmailException` handler mapping the exception to `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` (409), identical in shape to the neighbouring 409 handlers.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one added line invoking `DuplicateEmailException.rejectIfDuplicate(...)`, alongside the existing telephone/household reject calls.\n\nNo existing method's complexity grew meaningfully \u2014 the behaviour lives in a new cohesive unit, and each changed function stays trivially simple.",
